<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the Info.plist Xcode generates, for iOS and iPadOS only.
  Shepherd has one window: no second scene, on an iPad with Stage Manager
  either (docs/mobile-design.md, section 7). The scene manifest is this
  file's alone: the target doesn't generate one, which would say yes.

  The app's only encryption is SSH's, by standard algorithms (swift-crypto,
  swift-nio-ssh), and the App Store doesn't offer it in France, which would
  ask for a declaration of it: so no export compliance documents, and no
  question about them at each upload.

  A machine on the local network asks for the local network permission the
  first time the app connects to it, and so does a Mac whose QR code is
  scanned at a .local name or private IPv4 address. The camera is asked for
  the first time a Mac's QR code is scanned, by the app's own scanner. Both
  texts are translated in ShepherdMobile/InfoPlist.xcstrings.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>UIApplicationSceneManifest</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIApplicationSupportsMultipleScenes</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>hrdrhrdrhrdr connects over SSH to computers on your local network that you add.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>hrdrhrdrhrdr uses the camera to scan the QR code a Mac shows, to add that Mac.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
